// Wanted! - Sir Amik Varze, who is the one who takes the hat.
//
// Old School: "Return to Falador. Talk to Sir Amik Varze in the White Knights' Castle, and hand
// over the hat." Sir Tiffy hands out the commorb and the briefing and then has no part in the
// ending; this quest used to give him the whole of it.
//
// [opnpc1,sir_amik_varze] already exists in areas/area_falador and a trigger may only be declared
// once, so this hooks in the way Recipe for Disaster does there - by being asked for, rather than
// by running first and swallowing his other conversations. That mistake is written up in the
// comment at the top of his own script and is worth not repeating.

[proc,wanted_amik_wants]()(boolean)
if (%wanted_main = ^wanted_cornered) {
    return(true);
}
return(false);

[label,wanted_amik]
// The hat is the only one there will ever be - Solus is gone - so a hat dropped or lost on death
// would leave the quest one conversation from the end for good. Banked, he waits for it; gone,
// Savant can issue another, which is Old School's own answer: "If you lose Solus's hat, contact
// Savant for another one."
if (inv_total(inv, wanted_solus_trophy) = 0) {
    if (inv_total(bank, wanted_solus_trophy) > 0) {
        ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Then you have left it in a bank. Fetch it. I have waited eleven years; I can wait the afternoon.");
        return;
    }
    ~chatplayer("<p,sad>It's done. I've lost the hat, though.");
    ~chatnpc("<p,neutral>Then contact your handler on that orb and have her send another. I am not closing this on a story.");
    return;
}
~chatplayer("<p,neutral>It's done. Solus Dellagar is finished.");
if_close;
mes("Sir Amik turns the hat over twice and does not say anything for a while.");
p_delay(4);
~chatnpc("<p,sad>Eleven years. Eleven years and a hat.");
~chatnpc("<p,happy>You will forgive me if I do not make a speech. Consider yourself properly one of us.");
inv_del(inv, wanted_solus_trophy, 1);
@wanted_finish;

// THE REWARD IS SLAYER, AND IT IS ONE SKILL. This paid 18,000 Magic and 5,000 Hitpoints, and the
// quest pays neither: "1 Quest point, 5,000 Slayer experience, Access to the White Knights'
// armoury" and nothing else (oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Wanted!). A player noticed -
// DeathPlateau-Bugs#99.
//
// The 5,000 was the right NUMBER against the wrong SKILL, which is how this probably happened, and
// the 18,000 Magic has no source anywhere. Removing experience a player may already have banked is
// not something to do quietly, so it is said plainly on the issue.
//
// THE THIRD REWARD IS NOT PROMISED HERE, because this build has not got it. Old School's list ends
// with access to the White Knights' armoury, and [opnpc1,sir_vyvin] in areas/area_falador answers
// "Do you have anything to trade?" with "No, I'm sorry." - there is no armoury, and behind it in Old
// School sits a reputation system raised by killing Black Knights. Writing it on the completion
// scroll would be telling the player they have unlocked a shop that does not exist, so the scroll
// lists what they actually got. The missing reward is on DeathPlateau-Bugs#99 for Corey.
//
// Experience is in tenths here, as everywhere else in this repo - Fight Arena's
// stat_advance(attack, 121750) is Old School's own 12,175 - so 5,000 Slayer is 50000.
[label,wanted_finish]
%wanted_main = ^wanted_complete;
stat_advance(slayer, 50000);
session_log(^log_adventure, "Quest complete: Wanted!");
~send_quest_complete(questlist:wanted, wanted_solus_trophy, 200, ^wanted_questpoints, "You have completed\\nWanted!", "1 Quest Point|5,000 Slayer XP");
